Personal AI Playbook
A self-contained system for turning your best AI prompts into reusable workflows — instead of rewriting them from scratch every time.
Features
Workflows library — ready-made, editable prompt templates organized by category (daily build pipeline, debugging, consistency, prompt-engineering practice), each with fillable variables and a live preview
Prompt Builder — assemble custom prompts from labeled building blocks (role, objective, context, constraints, reasoning strategy, output format, tone, examples, quality checks) with a real-time preview
Loop Builder — convert any normal prompt into a self-evaluating autonomous loop by defining goals, evaluation criteria, improvement strategy, stop conditions, and safety rules
Learn — a plain-language glossary explaining every prompt-engineering concept used in the app, with weak vs. strong examples
Full CRUD on workflows: create, edit, duplicate, favorite, search, and filter
Dark/light mode, onboarding walkthrough, keyboard shortcuts, and JSON import/export
100% offline — all data saved to local storage, nothing leaves the browser
Tech Stack
HTML, CSS, vanilla JavaScript — zero external libraries, zero dependencies.
How to Run
Just open personal-ai-playbook.html in any browser. No server, no install.
What I Learned
Designing "building blocks" that are generic enough to combine into thousands of prompt variations — but still specific enough to teach why each piece matters — was harder than writing the prompts themselves.
Part of the #60DaysOfClaudeAI build-in-public challenge — Day 49.
